{note:Array: A data structure which saves elements like a list in many programming languages
This array needs to use all their elements be strings to simplify the calculus}

{note::array.init: Inits an array @constant,
@init {array} - []
@returns {Array}}
{set:array.init|[]}

{note::array(isString?,...items?): Inits an array @constructor
@param {[jsonifiedString]} items - Items in the array
@param {boolean} isString - Set this into true if the values of the array are already string}
{set:array()|{ignore:{set:array.__this|[{get:array(...items?)}]}{if:{get:array(isString?)}|!=|true|then:{note:You must work with [string] by default, so this won't be executed and won't waste iterations}{set:array.__this|[{substring:{foreach:{get:array.__this}|,{jsonify:{get:valuex}}}|1}]}}{get:array.__this}}}

{note::array.__safe: Get an safe version of the array which is escaped, @getter
@safe Removes all the escaped characters, replaces the brackets with keys and trims the keys at the corners,
Used to make calculus where the elements by theirself are not important, Not thought for normal work, 
@private
@returns {string} - Safe array}
{set:array.__safe|{ignore:{replace:\u007b|[|{replace:\u007d|]|{substring:{reverse:{substring:{reverse:{replace:\\.||{get:array.__this}}}|1}}|1}}}}}

{note::array.__trim: @getter @safe Trims the keys at the corners,
Used when the keys can break the operation, 
@private
@returns {string} - Safe array}
{set:array.__trim|{ignore:{substring:{reverse:{substring:{reverse:{replace:\\.||{get:array.__this}}}|1}}|1}}}

{note::array.length: Gets the length of an array @getter}
{set:array.length|{ignore:{set:array.length.safe|{eval:{get:array.__safe}}}{if:{get:array.length.safe}|=||then:0|else:{set:array.length.commaCount|{replace:[^,]||{replace:".+?"||{get:array.length.safe}}}}{length:{get:array.length.commaCount},}}{delete:array.length.safe}{delete:array.length.commaCount}}}

{note::array.at(index): Gets an item from the array at the index, but the index can be negative for looking at the end, @safe
@param {number} index - The index of the value in the array}
{set:array.at()|{ignore:
    {if:{get:array.at(index)}|>=|0|then:
        {set:retx|{traversejson:{get:array.at(index)}|{get:array.__this}}}
    |else:
        {set:array.at.length|{eval:{get:array.length}}}
        {set:retx|{traversejson:{len:{substring:{repeat:{get:array.at.length}|0}|{abs:{get:array.at(index)}}}}|{get:array.__this}}}
    }
    {delete:array.at(index)}
}}

{note::array.forEach(function,noWrap?,noString?): Iterates for each element-only array without using {foreach}, applying a function for each element, and returning an array-like with the output of each code, like .map() in JavaScript
Use {get:array.forEach(function).valuex} to get the value in each iteration, The value is not un-jsonified! (is still wrapped in the "")
@param {code} function - A function to iterate, we're assuming you've escaped the | in case you're going to use it outside a code block
@param {boolean} noWrap? - Prevent to escape the $ in the code
@param {boolean} noString? - Removes the "" at the start and end, and uses $1 instead of $&
This iteration method uses regexp to match every object in the string, using the replacer $& as the match.
Setting noWrap? into true will make that the $ in the code don't get escaped, so it's like replacing straightforward
Setting noString? into true doesn't un-jsonify the values, only removes the "" at the start and the end}
{set:array.forEach()|{ignore:
    {if:{get:array.forEach(noString?)}|=|true|then:
        {if:{get:array.forEach(noWrap?)}|=|true|then:
            {eval:{replace:(?<!\\\\)"(.*?)(?<!\\\\)"|in:{get:array.__this}|with:{get:array.forEach(function)}}}
        |else:
            {eval:{replace:(?<!\\\\)"(.*?)(?<!\\\\)"|in:{get:array.__this}|with:{ignore:{set:array.forEach(function).valuex|$1}} {replace:\$|$$$$|{get:array.forEach(function)}}}}
        }
    |else:
        {if:{get:array.forEach(noWrap?)}|=|true|then:
            {eval:{replace:(?<!\\\\)".*?(?<!\\\\)"|in:{get:array.__this}|with:{get:array.forEach(function)}}}
        |else:
            {eval:{replace:(?<!\\\\)".*?(?<!\\\\)"|in:{get:array.__this}|with:{ignore:{set:array.forEach(function).valuex|$&}} {replace:\$|$$$$|{get:array.forEach(function)}}}}
        }
    }
    {delete:array.forEach(noWrap?)} {delete:array.forEach(noString?)} {delete:array.forEach(function)}
    {delete:array.forEach(function).valuex}
}}

{note::array.slice(start,end?): Slices an array with a start and end (end exclusive)
@param {number} start - The position to start slicing
@param {number} end? - The position to end slicing, exclusive}
{set:array.slice()|{ignore:
    {if:{get:array.slice(end?)}|!=||then:
        {set:array.slice.length|{eval:{get:array.length}}}
    }
    {set:array.slice.trim|{eval:{get:array.__trim}}}
    {set:array.slice.sliced|{replace:{repeat:{get:array.slice(start)}|".*?"(?<!\\\\),}(.*)|$1|{get:array.slice.trim}}}
    {if:{get:array.slice(end?)}|!=||then:
        {set:array.slice.indexEnd|{len:{substring:{repeat:{get:array.slice.length}|,}|{get:array.slice(end?)}}}}
        {set:array.slice.sliced|{reverse:{replace:{repeat:{get:array.slice.indexEnd}|".*?"(?<!\\\\),}(.*)|$1|{reverse:{get:array.slice.sliced}}}}}        
    }
    {set:retx|[{get:array.slice.sliced}]}
    {delete:{get:array.slice(end?)}} {delete:array.slice(start)}
    {delete:array.slice.length} {delete:array.slice.sliced} {delete:array.slice.trim} {delete:array.slice.indexEnd}
}}

{note::array.concat(array1,array2): Concats an array with another array @static
@param {[jsonifiedString]} array1 - The first array to concat
@param {[jsonifiedString]} array2 - The second array to concat}
{set:array.concat()|{ignore:
    {set:retx|{reverse:{substring:{reverse:{get:array.concat(array1)}}|1}},{substring:{get:array.concat(array2)}|1}}
}}
